From 2eabaff551ab52bf295d022b623fe2149dfa5939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:43:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] moe-cache: reset the pipelined used-list readback when a
 table is re-allocated

alloc_table_locked re-allocates used_dev / used_host / used_host2 on a re-arm, but used_pending and
used_toggle carried over.  The first moe_cache_promote_host after the re-arm then consumed a buffer no
readback had written (fresh pinned memory reads as zeros) and admitted expert 0 into slot 0 - in some of a
layer's tables but not the others, depending on each table's carried-over state.  Every later admission then
landed one slot further in those tables, so gate and up held the same experts in different slots, and the
fused gate+up redirect (which reads the up table's remap for both lanes) read the wrong gate expert for about
half the slots.  Seen with -sm tensor --n-cpu-moe 48 -ub 6144 and a 3072 MiB slab headroom: wrong but stable
greedy output after the warm-up's eviction/re-arm, a different sha on every server start.

Start the readback pipeline over on a (re)allocation and initialise used_dev to -1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
index b31214577..960045c5c 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
@@ -2271,7 +2271,14 @@ void alloc_table_locked(table_t & t, int slots) {
                 t.used_dev = nullptr;
             } else {
                 t.used_cap = (int64_t) used_cap;
+                (void) cudaMemset(t.used_dev, 0xff, used_cap * sizeof(int32_t));
             }
+            // A re-allocation (re-arm / re-size) starts the pipelined used-list readback over: no readback
+            // is in flight for these new buffers, so nothing may be consumed from them on the next promote.
+            // A carried-over `used_pending` made that promote read a never-written buffer and admit expert
+            // 0 into slot 0 of some of a layer's tables but not the others, shifting the layer's slot order.
+            t.used_pending = false;
+            t.used_toggle  = 0;
             // The deferred promotion is per table per token; pageable D2H/H2D staging made it ~60 us
             // per table.  Pinned staging cuts that by ~5x and keeps the promotion off the critical path.
             if (t.used_dev != nullptr && cudaMallocHost((void **) &t.used_host, used_cap * sizeof(int32_t)) != cudaSuccess) {
-- 
